exif: bound an IFD tree by the size of the EXIF buffer (CVE-2026-125180)

av_exif_parse_buffer() let every tag of an IFD tree point at the same value
bytes, so a small buffer could make the parser copy far more than it holds
(memory exhaustion through overlapping tags). The three master commits stop at an
IFD chain that loops, bound the number of parsed entries by the 12-byte records
the buffer can hold, and bound the value bytes of the tree by the buffer size.

Backport of FFmpeg master c69aff745431c73e546bdad988ec23f74c79979c (2026-10-12), 26bf8651a8d88f722598c90f6afe7067e9a296dd (2026-10-12), 30fff47764e59f02ac7868bb832ed51a88f949fd (PR 25408, merged 2026-11-06), not in n9.0.2.
The last commit needs the entries bound of the second, so all three are carried;
applied in order they are unchanged from master apart from hunk line numbers.

